# exec'd by revise_paper_v3.py: measured effect of the doubled negation marker on A, E and the 200-sample benchmark
NR = json.load(open(ROOT / "results/paper_checks/negation_AE_NQ_rerun/summary.json"))
A_, E_, N_ = NR["A"], NR["E"], NR["nq200_v3"]
assert A_["em_outcome_changes_fixed_vs_control"] == 0 and E_["em_outcome_changes_fixed_vs_control"] == 0
assert A_["control_cont_correct"] == A_["fixed_cont_correct"] and E_["control_cont_correct"] == E_["fixed_cont_correct"]
assert N_["control_em_correct"] == N_["fixed_em_correct"] == 0 and N_["fixed_cont_correct"] - N_["control_cont_correct"] == 1
rep("Correcting every affected case could change at most 8 of A’s answers (against G’s 46-case lead over A) and 4 of E’s (more than G’s 2-case lead over E, which was already not significant), and at most 1 of the 26 chunked-only exact-match wins on the benchmark, which would leave that difference significant (25 against 7, p = 0.002).",
    "For these rebuilt contexts and for the 7 benchmark samples the effect was measured and not only bounded: each affected context was generated twice with qwen2.5-coder:7b, with the doubled marker kept and with it removed, under the original prompt and decoding settings (the rebuilt contexts are not the original ones, so the comparison is between the two generations on the same rebuilt text). Removing the marker changed no exact-match or containment outcome in the %d contexts of A (%d correct under both) or the %d of E (%d correct under both), so G’s lead over A (46 cases) and over E (2 cases) is not affected by the marker. On the benchmark it changed no exact-match outcome (none of the 7 correct under either text) and turned one containment outcome from wrong to right (Précis v3 containment 141 becomes 142 of 200, against 159 for the chunked baseline), so the 26-against-7 exact-match comparison and its conclusion stand. The control generation on the unchanged benchmark text reproduced all 7 stored exact-match outcomes and 6 of the 7 stored answers."
    % (A_["affected_contexts"], A_["control_em_correct"], E_["affected_contexts"], E_["control_em_correct"]))
rep("and a regeneration check showed no change in any outcome that could be tested (Appendix B.4).",
    "and regenerating answers with the marker removed changed no exact-match outcome in any case that could be tested, including rebuilt contexts of variants A and E and 7 benchmark samples (Appendix B.4).")
